<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jimyōin line</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Jimyōin-tō</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Jimyōin line was a branch of the Japanese imperial family descended from Emperor Go-Fukakusa, rival to the Daikakuji line of his brother Emperor Kameyama. From the late 13th century the two lines contested the throne, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kamakura">Kamakura</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shogun">shogunate</a> arranged for them to alternate. After 1336 the Jimyōin emperors formed the Northern Court backed by the Ashikaga shoguns, and all later emperors of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> descend from them.</p></div>
